 my  organization I haven't talked to Jake in  a long time  the benefit of that relationship is Jake  is a real thought leader in my function  and you know connecting with Jake and  networking with Jake is really going to  help me identify some conferences that  that I might consider attending in my  field so in order for me to take action  what I'm going to do is reach out to  Jake and you know maybe say can we meet  at Starbucks and have a cup of coffee or  can we grab lunch sometime you know the  next couple of months to have this  networking career development type of  conversation so again just want to offer  up some some tips as it relates to what  you can do in your current role to help  you build your brand you know obviously  by my biggest piece of advice for folks  to to grow and advance their career is  to really do well in your current job  let's don't over look at that so again  make sure your ongoing dialogue with  your leaders and really understand the  goals and objectives associated with  your roles and in how your overall  performance is going to be measured you  know that happens through hopefully a  lot of ongoing discussion you're having  but certainly if your organization's  have formal review processes great  opportunity to do so I think it's  important to that you have that you  would really work to understand your  management your manager style and what  some of their pet peeves are so you can  so you can avoid those again  communication is key right so don't be  afraid to ask for feedback you know  don't make any false assumptions you  don't know what you don't know so make  sure you are an active participant in  that in that dialogue again building and  maintaining relationships both on the  personal and professional fun are key  network with your peers get their advice  in maintain those relationships and you  know step out there attend events or  volunteer in situations to get you  exposure to to new people you just never  know what that